#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/is.rc -- Icelandic (Íslenska), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "is"`.
//
// Stage E109, group B: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc; app.rc includes this file. An adaptation, not a literal
// translation (decision 198.14): the terms are those of l10n/glossary/is.tsv, the tone is the
// informal "þú" of Windows in Icelandic, the voice of the author is masculine ("glaður").
// Where each string is seen and how much room it has is res/lang/context.tsv.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Icelandic — `[general] language = "is"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
